<LegalLayout title="Privacy" description="What Aspiran collects on this website, why, and how to ask us to change or delete it." updated="November 2026">
  <p>
    This page covers the Aspiran website (aspiran.in). The Aspiran app will have its own privacy notice before it is released.
    Aspiran is run by [Legal entity name], [registered address].
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>What you tell Chotu.</b> As you scroll the home page, Chotu (our AI guide) asks a few questions: your name, which attempt this is, your medium, your optional, how many hours you study and similar. Your answers are saved to our server as you give them, under a random ID your browser makes. They are not linked to your name, phone or email unless you give us one.</li>
    <li><b>Your phone number or email, only if you tick the box.</b> We keep it only after you agree that we can message you about early access and the offer. Without the tick, it is not saved.</li>
    <li><b>Chats with Chotu.</b> If you type a question to Chotu, the conversation and your answers above are sent to an AI service to write the reply. Today that is Groq, Google (Gemini) or NVIDIA. They process it to answer you; we do not ask them to keep it. We do not store the chat text itself. Please don't type passwords, Aadhaar numbers or payment details.</li>
    <li><b>Daily limits.</b> To stop misuse, we count how many AI replies a device and a network get each day. For the network count we keep a scrambled code made from your internet address and the date, not the address itself, and it changes every day.</li>
    <li><b>What you send us on WhatsApp.</b> If you choose the WhatsApp button, a summary of your answers is placed into a message that you choose to send. We receive that message and your phone number, as with any WhatsApp chat.</li>
    <li><b>Visit statistics (only if switched on).</b> We may use Umami, a privacy-friendly analytics tool that does not use cookies. It records page views and which buttons are tapped, not who you are.</li>
    <li><b>On your device.</b> Your browser remembers the random ID, your answers to Chotu, and your language and light or dark choice, so a reload does not start over. You can clear this by clearing the site's data in your browser.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Our server and database run on Cloudflare.</p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <p>To answer your questions, to reply to you, to place you in a pod batch when the app opens, to tell you about early access and offers you asked about, and to understand which parts of the site help people.</p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell your data.</li>
    <li>We do not run advertising trackers on this site.</li>
    <li>Chotu is an AI. It does not predict ranks or results, and it never asks for passwords, Aadhaar or payment details.</li>
    <li>This service is for people aged 18 and over.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>[Retention period, for example: early-access chats are kept until the app launches and for 12 months after, then deleted].</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it (including what you told Chotu), by messaging +91 98766 56573 on WhatsApp.
    You can also stop us from contacting you by telling us to stop. These rights follow India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.
  </p>

  <h2>WhatsApp</h2>
  <p>WhatsApp is a separate service with its own privacy policy. Messages sent through it are handled under those terms as well as this page.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or complaints: [Grievance contact name], [email], +91 98766 56573.</p>
